{{!
    @template tool_dynamic_cohorts/matching_users

    A placeholder for the matching-users count of one rule. The count arrives over AJAX
    and the control opens the matching-users modal.

    Classes required for JS:
    * tool-dynamic-cohorts-matching-users - amd/src/manage_rules.js finds every instance,
      unhides the second child, appends the count inside the control it holds and binds
      the modal to that control.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-ruleid - the rule whose count is fetched.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * ruleid - ID of the rule.

    The control is a button, not a link: the click is handled entirely in JS and the count
    is appended after the visually hidden label, so the accessible name reads "Matching
    users: 1 234" rather than a bare number. A plain aria-label would have replaced the
    count instead of introducing it.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "ruleid": "10"
    }
}}
<div class="tool-dynamic-cohorts-matching-users" data-ruleid="{{ruleid}}">
    <span>{{#pix}} i/loading, core, {{#str}} loading {{/str}} {{/pix}}</span>
    <div class="hidden">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-link p-0 border-0 align-baseline"><span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}} matchingusers, tool_dynamic_cohorts {{/str}}: </span></button>
    </div>
</div>
